# {{ project.name }}

A mod for [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code). It puts a greeting in the status line and has a settings page with an on/off switch, the language and the greeting text.

## Install

Requires Claude Code with plugin support for function hooks and Node 24 or newer.

```bash
npm install
npm run types
```

Load the mod for one session:

```bash
claude --plugin-dir {% raw %}/absolute/path/to/{% endraw %}{{ project.slug }}
```

or in every session, through `env` in `~/.claude/settings.json` (then restart Claude Code):

```json
{ "env": { "CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS": "/absolute/path/to/{{ project.slug }}" } }
```

To turn it off, remove the folder from that list or type `/{{ project.slug }} off`.

Mods run with your permissions and are not sandboxed: read the code before you enable one.

## Use

- `/{{ project.slug }}` — status; `/{{ project.slug }} on` and `off`; `/{{ project.slug }} reload` — re-read the settings; `/{{ project.slug }} ui` — open the settings page.
- Settings are kept in `~/.claude/mod-data/{{ project.slug }}/config.json`.

## Develop

```bash
npm run dev      # settings page with hot reload: http://localhost:{{ ports.UI_DEV_PORT }}
npm run check    # lint, formatting, types, tests, build, Claude Code's own validation
```

See `AGENTS.md` for the structure and for how to add settings, hooks and commands.
